<title>SOUTH KOREA: Yukong temporarily shuts naphtha cracker.</title>
<headline>Yukong temporarily shuts naphtha cracker.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1996-10-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Yukong Ltd, South Korea's biggest refiner, closed its 400,000 tonnes a year naphtha cracker (NCC) on Sunday for annual maintenance, a company official said on Monday.</p>
<p>The cracker is scheduled to resume operation on November 23, he said.</p>
<p>Yukong is capable of cracking 570,000 tonnes of naphtha a year.</p>
<p>--Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5643</p>
</text>
